<edge source="global_bond_rout::financial_conditions" target="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A bond rout that tightens financial conditions raises trade‑finance and working‑capital costs for refiners, traders and shipping firms, leading to cutbacks in exports/shipments and higher diesel spot prices as near‑term supply is constrained.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d40">global_fuel_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::financial_conditions" target="us_china_rivalry::investment_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter financial conditions (wider spreads, reduced liquidity and higher borrowing costs) directly constrain credit lines, debt financing and IPO/exit windows that fund AI firms, causing a measurable drop in capital deployment to the AI sector.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
