</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::cross_border_flows" target="global_fuel_shock::diesel_import_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in cross‑border capital flows during a bond rout reduces availability of letters of credit and import financing for fuel buyers, directly lowering diesel import volumes into capital‑constrained markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d40">global_fuel_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::cross_border_flows" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden pullback in cross-border capital and trade finance reduces working capital for energy traders and delays payments for maintenance and shipments, producing immediate interruptions and bottlenecks in regional gas and fuel deliveries linked to the Russia–Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::cross_border_flows" target="us_china_rivalry::semiconductor_supply" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Reductions in cross‑border private and public capital flows and foreign investment delay or cancel funding for greenfield fabs and equipment purchases, reducing near‑term expansion of advanced semiconductor manufacturing capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
