<edge source="mideast_escalation::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_bond_rout::long_nominal_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Sudden removal or delay of crude/refined flows raises global energy prices and near-term inflation expectations and forces a higher term premium as investors demand compensation for elevated inflation and geopolitical risk, pushing long-dated government yields up.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_fuel_shock::diesel_supply_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Physical damage to refineries, pipeline closures or seizure of export facilities in the Middle East immediately removes refined diesel volumes from international shipments, reducing the rate of diesel entering global markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_fuel_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::energy_supply_disruption" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Outages or shipment losses in Middle Eastern crude/LNG and refined products reduce global available supply to European and global markets, driving up wholesale energy prices that directly raise the energy price level relevant to the Russia–Ukraine theatre.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::energy_supply_disruption" target="us_china_rivalry::semiconductor_supply" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Interruptions to crude/refined product flows cause fuel and power shortages for energy‑intensive fabs and their emergency generation, resulting in immediate curtailment of manufacturing throughput.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::oil_price_volatility" target="mideast_escalation::market_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d28">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::oil_price_volatility" target="global_bond_rout::financial_conditions" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Large, abrupt oil-price swings increase market volatility and credit/spread risk, prompting wider lending spreads, higher margin requirements and reduced market liquidity, which tightens overall financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::oil_price_volatility" target="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp swings in crude and refined-product prices raise risk premia, impair market-making and prompt short-term speculative and precautionary bids, producing upward pressure and spikes in diesel spot market prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_fuel_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="mideast_escalation::oil_price_volatility" target="us_china_rivalry::investment_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Large short‑term swings in oil prices raise macroeconomic and cost‑of‑capital uncertainty for investors and energy‑dependent data centers, leading venture and corporate investors to slow or reallocate new funding away from high‑risk AI ventures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">mideast_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
