<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_bond_rout::fiscal_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Interruptions to energy deliveries force governments to fund emergency subsidies, price caps and strategic purchases/stockpiles, widening deficits and increasing near‑term sovereign fiscal stress.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_fuel_shock::diesel_supply_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Direct damage to refineries, port closures, export bans or interdictions tied to the war reduce the volume of diesel that exporters can deliver to international markets, cutting the global diesel supply rate.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_fuel_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Interruptions to production and export logistics raise delivery risk and create localized prompt shortages that producers and traders price into spot markets, pushing up diesel spot prices in major hubs.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_fuel_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_disruption" target="mideast_escalation::maritime_transit_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Interruptions to Russian energy flows lead buyers to redirect crude and product shipments toward Middle Eastern suppliers, increasing tanker traffic through chokepoints (e.g., Bab al‑Mandeb, Suez) and thereby raising the probability and impact of maritime disruptions or attacks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_escalation</data>
</edge>
