<edge source="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" target="global_bond_rout::long_nominal_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in diesel spot prices increases headline and core inflation expectations and the inflation risk premium, causing investors to demand higher yields on long-dated government debt.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" target="global_bond_rout::financial_conditions" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher diesel prices push up input costs and inflation, prompting central banks to tighten policy and raising borrowing costs and credit spreads, which directly tightens aggregate financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" target="mideast_escalation::regional_security_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp diesel price spikes raise household and transport costs in fuel-importing economies, triggering protests, strikes and increased smuggling that elevate the frequency and intensity of local and cross-border security incidents.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" target="mideast_escalation::oil_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Large, rapid moves in diesel spot prices force refiners and traders to change crude slates, hedges and shipment schedules, generating amplified short-term swings in broader oil and refined-product prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" target="russia_ukraine_war::inflation_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising diesel spot prices increase transport and input costs for food and goods across the affected economies, directly feeding through to consumer prices and raising measured inflation rates in the short term.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_fuel_shock::diesel_spot_price" target="us_china_rivalry::investment_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp increases in diesel spot prices raise operational and logistics costs for data centers, training runs, and hardware supply chains, compressing near-term returns and leading investors to pull back or reallocate capital away from AI projects with tight margins.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_rivalry</data>
</edge>
